                        "review": "I really liked the start of this game. Sci-fi setting, nice cozy yurt, trying to put a giant puzzle together. All things that make up games I like. Sadly, the gameplay quickly killed and detracted any good those aspects brought. \n\nGrabbing objects and using them has been a challenge. It was quite clunky. A few times I dropped objects and could hardly find them. Using items could be like having toddler arms where order of use matters. Furthermore, the cube games required a lot of finesse in moving objects which toddler arms don't seem to like. \n\nThough I could not motivate myself to make it to the end, I could see how if one has the patience or natural skill to navigate with the controls, the story seemed like it had a lot of potential. The environment seemed to be there. I just can't say for sure as I did not have the will to keep playing.",
